The FlowStep constructor requires a goal string and optionally a plugins factory delegate. It has Provides, Requires, and Passthrough collections that can be populated via AddProvides, AddRequires, and AddPassthrough methods.

The Flow constructor requires a name and a goal string and inherits from FlowStep. It has a Steps list and AddStep method.

The FlowExecutor class is internal, so I cannot instantiate it directly in the test. I will create a public wrapper class in the test to expose the internal FlowExecutor for testing. I will also mock dependencies and create a Flow with a step that triggers the exit loop logging.

I will submit a test file with these adjustments.

